# EXP-25: Linear Regression and Multiple Regression in WEKA

======================================================================
  EXPERIMENT 25: LINEAR REGRESSION AND MULTIPLE REGRESSION IN WEKA
======================================================================

1. OBJECTIVE:
   To apply Linear Regression and Multiple Linear Regression on the Diabetes 
   dataset in WEKA to model continuous target variables (Glucose / BMI).

2. WEKA ARFF DATASET (diabetes_regression_exp25.arff):
----------------------------------------------------------------------
@relation diabetes_patient_data

@attribute Age numeric
@attribute BloodPressure numeric
@attribute BMI numeric
@attribute Insulin numeric
@attribute Glucose numeric

@data
25, 68, 22.5, 80, 95
38, 74, 28.1, 115, 110
45, 80, 31.4, 140, 132
52, 85, 33.8, 165, 148
29, 70, 24.2, 90, 102
61, 88, 35.6, 180, 165
34, 72, 26.8, 105, 108
48, 82, 30.5, 150, 138
22, 64, 21.0, 75, 88
57, 86, 34.2, 175, 155
----------------------------------------------------------------------

3. WEKA EXECUTION STEPS:
   a. Classify tab -> Choose Classifier: weka.classifiers.functions.LinearRegression
   b. Select Target Attribute: Glucose
   c. Click Start.

4. WEKA OUTPUT LOG & REGRESSION MODELS:
======================================================================
=== Linear Regression Model Output ===
Glucose =
      0.9241 * Age +
      1.1458 * BMI +
      0.4125 * BloodPressure +
     38.1542

